      "retained": "All six ratio-of-median and paired-median changes are negative. Four conditions have descriptive paired intervals wholly below zero (small fixed, medium fixed/canvas, large fixed). Small canvas and large canvas remain directionally inconclusive under observed paired variation.",
      "source": "All six paired medians are positive. Three intervals exclude zero upward: small fixed, medium fixed, large canvas. These are repeated within-run slowdowns on unchanged source paths and cannot be dismissed as random noise. Binary layout/JIT/instance or shared-heap effects are possible explanations, not established causes.",
      "parse": "Five of six ratio-of-median changes are positive; five of six paired medians are positive (not the same five). Small fixed is a supported upward shift with a very wide interval. Other five intervals include zero, so large parse +3.08/+4.77 percent median regressions are unresolved, not disproven. Medium canvas illustrates estimator sensitivity: ratio-of-medians -2.39 percent versus paired median +2.03 percent.",
      "decision": "Supports some retained browser improvement alongside observed source and small-parse regressions in this diagnostic. Does not support an across-the-board win or a no-regressions statement. Preserve this tradeoff in adoption reporting; full release gate remains separate.",
      "scope": "One Chromium/EPYC VM run, three Gantt sizes, two measurers, one-second warmup, fifteen balanced trials. No Safari/Firefox/Swift performance inference."
